{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.DescartesEllipticCurve","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.DescartesEllipticCurve","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.golden_ratio_degeneration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.golden_ratio_degeneration","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-elliptic-curve.lean#L118-L165","doc":"**Golden-ratio degeneration of `r(q)`.**  At `q = 1/φ²` the factor\n`(s² + s − 1)` vanishes, so `r(q) = 0` (cusp).\n\n**Was an axiom; proved 2026-09-04.**  The `rpow` occurrences are the only\nreal obstacle and they all collapse at this `q`: with `φ² = φ + 1` we have\n`q = (1/φ)²`, hence `q ^ (1/2) = 1/φ` by `Real.sqrt_sq`,\n`q ^ (3/2) = q · (1/φ)` by `Real.rpow_add`, and `q ^ (−1/2) = φ` by\n`Real.rpow_neg`.  What remains is a polynomial identity in `√5` that is\n*exactly* zero once `√5 ^ n` is reduced for `n = 2 … 6` — both the rational\npart and the `√5` part cancel, which is the algebraic content of `s − s⁻¹\n= −1` at the golden section. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.classical_limit_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.classical_limit_p","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-elliptic-curve.lean#L106-L113","doc":"At the classical limit q = 1, the curve degenerates to\ny² = x³ + (2/3)x + 20/27. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_elliptic_curve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartes_elliptic_curve","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-elliptic-curve.lean#L70-L104","doc":"**Color-cubic ↦ Weierstrass substitution.**\n\n**Was an axiom; proved 2026-11-15.** With `s = q^{1/2} > 0` we have\n`s² = q`, `q^{3/2} = q·s` and `q^{-1/2} = s⁻¹`; after that the two\nidentities are rational-function identities in `s`, closed by\n`field_simp; ring`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:descartes-elliptic-curve","label":"prop:descartes-elliptic-curve","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-elliptic-curve.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.j_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.j_invariant","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-elliptic-curve.lean#L54-L58","doc":"The j-invariant of a Weierstrass curve `y² = x³ + px + r`:\n`j = -1728·(4p)³ / Δ`, where `Δ` is the `weierstrass_discriminant`\n`-16(4p³ + 27r²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_discriminant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_discriminant","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-elliptic-curve.lean#L50-L52","doc":"The discriminant Δ of a Weierstrass curve y² = x³ + px + r. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_r","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-elliptic-curve.lean#L40-L48","doc":"The second Weierstrass coefficient r(q) of the Descartes elliptic curve.\n\nr(q) = 20(q-1)³/(27q^{3/2}) + 5(q-1)²/(9q) + 5(√q - 1/√q)/9 + 20/27 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_p","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-elliptic-curve.lean#L33-L38","doc":"The first Weierstrass coefficient p(q) of the Descartes elliptic curve.\n\np(q) = 2(q² - q + 1)/(3q) + (q - 1)/(3√q) ","signatureChunk":0}]}